<sect2 xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" id="gimp-filter-gaussian-blur">
  <title>Desfoque Gaussiano</title>

  <indexterm>
    <primary>Filtros</primary>
    <secondary>Desfocar</secondary>
    <tertiary>Desfoque Gaussiano</tertiary>
  </indexterm>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Desfoque Gaussiano</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <sect3>
    <title>Visão geral</title>
    <figure>
      <title>Exemplo para o filtro <quote>Desfoque Gaussiano</quote></title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="JPG" fileref="images/filters/examples/taj_orig.jpg"/>
        </imageobject>
        <caption>
          <para>Imagem original</para>
        </caption>
      </mediaobject>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="JPG" fileref="images/filters/examples/blur-taj-gauss.jpg"/>
        </imageobject>
        <caption>
          <para>Filter applied</para>
        </caption>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
    <para>
      The Gaussian Blur filter acts on each pixel of the active layer or
      selection, setting its Value to the average of all pixel Values present
      in a radius defined in the dialog. A higher Value will produce a higher
      amount of blur. The blur can be set to act in one direction more than
      the other by clicking the Chain Button so that it is broken, and
      altering the radius. GIMP supports two implementations of Gaussian Blur:
      FIR and IIR. They both produce the same results, but each one can be
      faster in some cases. They are complemented by the default Auto setting,
      that automatically picks the optimal choice.
    </para>
  </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Ativando o filtro</title>
    <para>
      This filter is found in the main menu under
      <menuchoice>
        <guimenu>Filters</guimenu>
        <guisubmenu>Blur</guisubmenu>
        <guimenuitem>Gaussian Blur…</guimenuitem>
      </menuchoice>.
    </para>
  </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Opções</title>
    <figure>
      <title>Configurações dos parâmetros do filtro <quote>Desfoque Gaussiano</quote></title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/blur/gauss-options.png"/>
        </imageobject>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Presets</term>
        <term><quote>Input Type</quote></term>
        <term>Clipping</term>
        <term>Blending Options</term>
        <term>Preview</term>
        <term>Merge filter</term>
        <term>Split view</term>
        <listitem>
          <xi:include href="../about-common-features.xml"/>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term>Tamanho X</term>
        <term>Tamanho Y</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>Aqui, você pode definir a intensidade do desfoque. Ao alterar a proporção entre os desfoques horizontal e vertical, você pode criar o efeito de um desfoque de movimento.</para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term>Filtro</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Here you can select the filter type.
          </para>

          <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
              <term>Auto</term>
              <listitem>
                <para>
                  Try to select the best filter automatically. In most cases
                  this default is best left alone.
                </para>
              </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
              <term>FIR</term>
              <listitem>
                <para>Stands for <quote>Finite Impulse Response</quote>.
                </para>
              </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
              <term>IIR</term>
              <listitem>
                <para>Stands for <quote>Infinite Impulse Response</quote>.
                </para>
              </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
          </variablelist>

        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term>Política do Abismo</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>Política do Abismo (gerenciamento de bordas) é tratada com <xref linkend="abyss-policy"/>.</para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term>Cortar para a extensão da entrada</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>Se a extensão da saída deve ser cortada para os limites da entrada: esta opção remove pixels indesejados criados nas bordas pelo desfoque.</para>
          <figure>
            <title>Exemplo</title>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/blur/clip-orig.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>
                <para>Canto superior direito da imagem, ampliação x800</para>
              </caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/blur/clip-0.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>
                <para><quote>Cortar para a extensão da entrada</quote> desmarcado</para>
              </caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/blur/clip-1.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>
                <para><quote>Cortar para a extensão da entrada</quote> marcado</para>
              </caption>
            </mediaobject>
          </figure>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
    <para>O filtro de Desfoque Gaussiano não preserva bordas na imagem: <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/blur/median-vs-gaussian.png"/>
        </imageobject>
        <caption>
          <para>
            Left: Original image
          </para>
          <para>
            Middle: <link linkend="gimp-filter-median-blur">Median Blur</link> filter applied
          </para>
          <para>
            Right: <link linkend="gimp-filter-gaussian-blur">Gaussian Blur</link> filter applied
          </para>
        </caption>
      </mediaobject></para>
  </sect3>
</sect2>
